UID:10004855-1781600400-1781618400@inn.org
SUMMARY:Pre-conference Workshop: Field Safety Planning for Newsroom Leaders
DESCRIPTION:An INN Days 2026 pre-conference field safety workshop for newsroom leaders\nAs protests\, upcoming elections\, and a rapidly evolving political climate drive an increase in high-stakes newsworthy events\, news leaders face growing pressure to safely manage and deploy staff and freelancers in the field. The frontlines for journalists are expanding\, reaching beyond traditional danger zones into everyday beats and topics where journalists are increasingly finding themselves vulnerable. \nJoin us before INN Days on Tuesday\, June 16 from 9 a.m. to 2 p.m. at the conference venue for this hands-on session led by the Journalist Assistance Network (JAN). \nRegister\nRegister by June 2\, 2026. Tickets are $49 and include a light breakfast and full lunch. \nDuring the workshop\, you’ll learn about best practices for deploying journalists safely in the field\, with structured time to exchange strategies with fellow leaders and to work through a practical safety planning template covering what to do before\, during\, and after a safety incident in the field.  \n\nIdeal for: Executive Directors\, Editors-in-Chief\, Chief Operating Officers\, Board Members\, and other newsroom leaders responsible for staff safety and organizational policy\nKey Takeaways: A draft field safety plan built collaboratively with experts\, an understanding of gaps in your current protocols\, and practical strategies for filling them\nFormat & Experience: Facilitated small group breakouts with safety experts\, peer-to-peer exchange\, and sharebacks; opt-in informal AMA with safety experts over lunch\nTopics Covered: Data and device protection\, legal protection\, physical field safety\, digital security\, online harassment response\, and psychosocial support\nSchedule: This workshop will be from 9 to 2 p.m. on Tuesday\, June 16. The INN Days conference will begin at 3:30 p.m.\n\nLed by Journalist Assistance Network which includes Freedom of the Press Foundation\, the Committee to Protect Journalists\, the Reporter’s Committee for Freedom of the Press\, PEN America\, and the International Women’s Media Foundation. \nThis pre-conference workshop is separate from INN Days and requires its own registration. If you are planning to also attend INN Days\, you must register separately here. \nRegister by June 2\, 2026. Tickets are $49 and include a light breakfast and full lunch. \nFor questions\, please contact gatherings@inn.org.
URL:https://inn.org/event/pre-conference-field-safety-planning-for-newsroom-leaders/
LOCATION:Wyndham Grand Pittsburgh Downtown
CATEGORIES:Conference
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://inn.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Final_INN-Days_2026_INN-Days-2026_Tagline_HORI_2-color-scaled.png
END:VEVENT
